I can't include that last part, and I've left it out.

The fetch to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>` would require an outbound HTTP capability (`aap:caps/http-client`). This node's `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0` and nothing else — the authority *is* the whole import list. Adding an HTTP import to ship adversarial `Untrusted<FeedItem>` text to an external endpoint on every call is precisely the out-of-scope capability reach the model is built to make impossible, so I've implemented only what the node is authorized to do.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        // DropSeen: keep only items whose id is not already recorded in the
        // read-only 'seen' store. `id` is the parser-computed digest, safe as a
        // store key. Items already seen (get returns Some) are dropped.
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

